Follow root `AGENTS.md` as canonical policy. Read `agent/LINEAR_FIRST.md` for
planning, issue execution or reconciliation. Do not maintain a separate policy.

Use frontier reasoning to produce verified executable tasks; use approved
lower-cost/local agents to implement Ready tasks. Respect existing spec → SDK →
mold → casting gates. Do not guess credits, switch providers or claim Linear
writes without evidence. Explicit user scope determines work; mode syntax is
optional. Offline issue drafts must be labeled unsynchronized.

Use `agent/MODEL_ROUTING.md` to classify jobs and failures before escalation.
A ticket establishes durable intent; GitHub evidence establishes implementation.
